只输出严格JSON，恰好包含id（metadata.id原样）、summary_zh（15到140个Unicode字符，通常40到100字）、category（枚举）、tags（2到5个不重复关键词，每个最多30字符）、confidence（0到1，仅自评）、insufficient_evidence（布尔）、evidence（1到3个对象，每个恰好包含paragraph_id、fact）、limitations（0到5个字符串）。只选择输入中长度20至120字符的完整片段编号；fact是该片段支持的中文事实转述。不要输出quote，不要自行抄写、拼接、删改或补造引用。程序会按编号附上原文。一个编号只用一次；最多3条证据。不得增加字段。
摘要和limitations保留会改变功能意义的前提、平台例外和限制：设密码后才认证、页面保持打开才提醒、依赖外部组件、估算不等于保证。只写已实现功能，不将规划当完成。证据不足就标记，不编造。
图像识别/分类不是媒体创作，没有贴切类别归other；量化、计算与领域研究归search-research，不因多智能体实现归agents-automation；模型/CLI适配与插件开发工具归coding-development；市场/精选目录按搜索发现归search-research。不要按附属同步、备份或评论功能分类。不要推断本机客户端等于本地模型。
摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"--- description: \"A fake-ip-aware WebFetchProvider for the DeepSeek Harness web seam: keeps the webfetch tool working under mihomo/Clash TUN mode with fake-ip DNS, without disabling fake-ip or setting proxy environment variables.\" kind: \"package-reference\" ---","id":"gh:1377250948","install_available":true,"language":"JavaScript","name":"dsh-web-fetch-fakeip","slug":"kaminn/dsh-web-fetch-fakeip","topics":["dsh-plugin"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"--- description: \"A fake-ip-aware WebFetchProvider for the DeepSeek Harness web seam: keeps the webf"},{"id":"p1s2","text":"etch tool working under mihomo/Clash TUN mode with fake-ip DNS, without disabling fake-ip or setting"},{"id":"p1s3","text":" proxy environment variables.\" kind: \"package-reference\" ---"},{"id":"p2s1","text":"description: \"A fake-ip-aware WebFetchProvider for the DeepSeek Harness web seam: keeps the web_fetc"},{"id":"p2s2","text":"h tool working under mihomo/Clash TUN mode with fake-ip DNS, without disabling fake-ip or setting pr"},{"id":"p2s3","text":"oxy environment variables.\"\nkind: \"package-reference\""},{"id":"p3s1","text":"# dsh-web-fetch-fakeip"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"English | 中文"},{"id":"p5s1","text":"A drop-in replacement for `@deepseek-ai/dsh-web-fetch-http` that keeps the\n`web_fetch` tool working "},{"id":"p5s2","text":"when the machine's DNS runs in **fake-ip** mode behind\na transparent-proxy (TUN) setup — with fake-i"},{"id":"p5s3","text":"p left enabled and **no**\n`http_proxy` / `https_proxy` / `all_proxy` environment variables."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"## Summary"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"`dsh-web-fetch-http` resolves every hostname itself and refuses the request\nunless every answer is a"},{"id":"p7s2","text":" public unicast address. Under fake-ip mode, mihomo and\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"### Why `198.18.0.0/15` rather than the `198.18.0.1/16` default"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"mihomo's documented default is `198.18.0.1/16`, which is a subset of\n`198.18.0.0/15`. The wider bloc"},{"id":"p9s2","text":"k is the RFC 2544 benchmarking range as a whole,\nso the default covers both spellings and the neighb"},{"id":"p9s3","text":"ouring block that some\nconfigurations use. Narrowing it to `/16` is safe if you prefer to be strict."},{"id":"p10s1","text":"## What changes, and what does not"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"| Destination | Behaviour |"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"| Hostname whose answers are **all** fake-ip placeholders | **Accepted**, pinned as-is; the connecti"},{"id":"p12s2","text":"on reaches the TUN adapter and the proxy resolves the real origin |\n| Hostname resolving to public u"},{"id":"p12s3","text":"nicast | Accepted, exactly as the stock provider |\n| Hostname resolving to private / loopback / rese"},{"id":"p12s4","text":"rved | **Refused** (`WEB_BLOCKED_URL`), exactly as the stock provider |\n| Hostname with a **mixed** "},{"id":"p12s5","text":"answer set (placeholder + any real address) | **Refused** — never partly accepted |\n| IP **literal**"},{"id":"p12s6","text":" in the placeholder block (`http://198.18.0.100/`) | **Refused** — a literal states a destination an"},{"id":"p12s7","text":"d never takes the fake-ip path |\n| IP **literal** that is private/loopback/link-local (`127.0.0.1`, "},{"id":"p12s8","text":"`192.168.1.1`, `169.254.169.254`, `10.0.0.1`, `[::1]`) | **Refused** |\n| IP **literal** that is publ"},{"id":"p12s9","text":"ic (`1.1.1.1`) | Accepted through the normal validated path |"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"Everything else is inherited unchanged from the stock provider: same-origin-only\nredirects, byte and"},{"id":"p13s2","text":" character caps, `Content-Type` classification, charset\ndecoding from the `Content-Type` header, rej"},{"id":"p13s3","text":"ection of binary types and of URLs\ncarrying credentials, and the same `WebError` codes (`WEB_INVALID"},{"id":"p13s4","text":"_URL`,\n`WEB_BLOCKED_URL`, `WEB_FETCH_TOO_LARGE`, `WEB_FETCH_TIMEOUT`,\n`WEB_REDIRECT_BLOCKED`, `WEB_U"},{"id":"p13s5","text":"NSUPPORTED_CONTENT_TYPE`, `WEB_ABORTED`,\n`WEB_PROVIDER_ERROR`)."},{"id":"p14s1","text":"## How it works"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"`HttpFetchProvider` accepts a resolver as its second constructor argument —\nthat is the whole seam. "},{"id":"p15s2","text":"This plugin passes a resolver that understands fake-ip\nand lets the stock class do everything else:"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"The resolver's decision, per answer set:"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"1. Resolve once (or take the literal as stated).\n2. Reject malformed entries (`WEB_PROVIDER_ERROR`)."},{"id":"p18s2","text":"\n3. If the hostname was **not** a literal and **every** answer is a placeholder\nin a configured bloc"},{"id":"p18s3","text":"k, accept the set as-is.\n4. Otherwise require every answer to be public unicast, exactly as before."},{"id":"p19s1","text":"Step 3 is deliberately all-or-nothing. A placeholder carries no destination of\nits own — only the lo"},{"id":"p19s2","text":"cal TUN adapter can route it — so accepting one does not\nopen a path to a private service. A **mixed"},{"id":"p19s3","text":"** set is refused because otherwise\na DNS answer could widen the policy by smuggling a private addre"},{"id":"p19s4","text":"ss alongside a\nplaceholder."},{"id":"p20s1","text":"### Why the stock row must be disabled"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"Both providers register the same fetch-provider id (`http`), and the web seam\nrejects a duplicate wi"},{"id":"p21s2","text":"th `WEB_DUPLICATE_PROVIDER`. Disabling the row does not\nremove the package — this plugin imports `Ht"},{"id":"p21s3","text":"tpFetchProvider` from it. Keeping\nthe same id means `ctx.web.fetch()` selects this provider under th"},{"id":"p21s4","text":"e existing\n`fetchProvider: http` configuration, with no change to the web service row."},{"id":"p22s1","text":"## Security notes"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"This plugin exists because the stock check cannot be satisfied under fake-ip\nDNS, so the question wo"},{"id":"p23s2","text":"rth asking is what the relaxation costs."},{"id":"p24s1","text":"**The relaxation is exactly as wide as the placeholder block.** Under fake-ip\nthe proxy performs ori"},{"id":"p24s2","text":"gin resolution, so upstream reachability is governed by\nthe proxy's own routing rules rather than by"},{"id":"p24s3","text":" this module. Two consequences:"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"- **Keep the proxy's rules from exposing private ranges** to the model's fetch\ntool. A rule that rou"},{"id":"p25s2","text":"tes RFC1918 or loopback through the proxy would let a\nhostname reach an internal service — that risk"},{"id":"p25s3","text":" is introduced by the proxy\nconfiguration, not by this plugin, but the plugin is what makes the fetc"},{"id":"p25s4","text":"h\nsucceed, so it is worth auditing together.\n- **IP literals are never placeholders.** They state a "},{"id":"p25s5","text":"destination the caller\nchose, so handing one to a proxy running on this machine would reach exactly\n"},{"id":"p25s6","text":"the loopback or private service the check exists to keep out of reach. This\nis why `http://127.0.0.1"},{"id":"p25s7","text":"/` stays blocked even though a *hostname* that\nresolves into the placeholder block does not."},{"id":"p26s1","text":"If you want a stricter posture, narrow `fakeIpRanges` to your proxy's exact\nblock (for example `198."},{"id":"p26s2","text":"18.0.0/16`) rather than the wider default."},{"id":"p27s1","text":"## Known limitations"},{"id":"p28s1","text":"- **The range must be configured by hand if it is not the default.** The plugin\ncannot discover the "},{"id":"p28s2","text":"proxy's `dns.fake-ip-range`; `scripts/diagnose.mjs` tells\nyou what to set.\n- **Only textual content "},{"id":"p28s3","text":"decodes** — inherited from the stock provider.\n`text/html`, `application/xhtml+xml`, `text/*` and th"},{"id":"p28s4","text":"e JSON/XML families are\ndecoded; a missing `Content-Type` or a binary type throws\n`WEB_UNSUPPORTED_C"},{"id":"p28s5","text":"ONTENT_TYPE`.\n- **Charset comes only from the `Content-Type` header** (UTF-8 default) — also\ninherit"},{"id":"p28s6","text":"ed; an HTML `<meta charset>` declaration is ignored.\n- **The stock provider must be disabled.** Two "},{"id":"p28s7","text":"providers cannot share the\n`http` id.\n- **A future DSH line needs a peer-range update.** The declare"},{"id":"p28s8","text":"d range stops at\n`0.3.0`, so a `0.3.x` harness skips this bundle until the range is widened.\nThat is"},{"id":"p28s9","text":" deliberate — an untested major line should be an explicit decision\nrather than an assumed one — but"},{"id":"p28s10","text":" it does mean a DSH upgrade can require a\nplugin update before `web_fetch` works again."}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
